      "side": 1,
      "message": "Julio: I found this question on a piece of paper I wrote. I\u0027m sorry I didn\u0027t ask you this question until now.\n\nThe `buf[dst_idx][0] \u0026 crc_mask` part of this statement takes the lower 16 bits of a CRC32 checksum as the hash table bucket index. Do you think we should consider the upper 16 bits when generating the hash table bucket index?\n\nIntuitively this is not necessary if CRC32 has thoroughly mixed the input data into all 32 bits of its output.",
      "revId": "e91b7aa26d6d0979bba2bee5e1c27a7a695e0226",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49487bd1_0ddb2090",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/hash_motion.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 476,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-05T01:09:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s necessary to consider the upper 16 bits for the hash table bucket index. The bits are reasonably mixed so taking a subset is fine for encoding purposes w.r.t. speed and compression performance (on non-adversarial inputs).\n\nHowever, there\u0027s something to keep in mind: because CRC32 isn\u0027t a cryptographic hash, a user can construct a specific input such as its pixels cause an increase in the number of block collisions during the hashing process. Not considering all CRC32 bits for the hash table index would technically make the task of finding collisions a bit easier (not by much in the grand scheme of things).\n\nThat said, because of our new hash table bucket size limitation/pruning mitigations in place, the encoder would just slow down by a bit on adversarial inputs in practice (vs. by a lot in previous libaom versions, where there wasn\u0027t an actual upper bound on how many elements a hash table bucket can have).",
      "parentUuid": "828075a5_288d9de7",
      "revId": "e91b7aa26d6d0979bba2bee5e1c27a7a695e0226",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
